+- **The run form's name.** `«…亡不绝者生不绝»` brings in 不绝. The grammar's word for "at arbitrarily late steps" is 屡 (`«屡»`, `«或屡»`, GrammarLaws.lean:1569). Propose `«定后前者在前则亡屡者生屡»` to GrammarLaws' owner, or say why 不绝.
